1
00:00:03,350 --> 00:00:06,423
Properties are YAML files that sit next to your SQL.

2
00:00:06,703 --> 00:00:12,766
They describe models, seeds and sources: what a table is, what each column means, and later, the tests.

3
00:00:13,716 --> 00:00:16,102
We already have one: sources dot yml.

4
00:00:16,382 --> 00:00:21,489
Today we add schema dot yml for the models, and seeds dot yml for the zone lookup.

5
00:00:22,439 --> 00:00:23,624
Open the project.

6
00:00:23,904 --> 00:00:26,795
In models, create a new file: schema dot yml.

7
00:00:32,304 --> 00:00:33,847
It is long, so paste it.

8
00:00:34,127 --> 00:00:39,051
One entry per model: a name, a description, and the columns that need explaining.

9
00:00:39,331 --> 00:00:41,284
The code is in the repository.

10
00:00:42,234 --> 00:00:45,323
For example, payment type: one means credit card.

11
00:00:45,603 --> 00:00:49,098
Anyone reading the model learns that here, not from a PDF.

12
00:00:49,378 --> 00:00:49,978
Save.

13
00:00:50,928 --> 00:00:51,790
Now the seed.

14
00:00:52,070 --> 00:00:54,565
In seeds, a new file: seeds dot yml.

15
00:00:59,216 --> 00:01:04,550
This one is short: the zone lookup, where it comes from, and its key column, Location ID.

16
00:01:04,830 --> 00:01:05,429
Save.

17
00:01:08,657 --> 00:01:11,695
Descriptions can also go into the database itself.

18
00:01:11,975 --> 00:01:16,328
Open dbt project dot yml, and add a models block at the end.

19
00:01:17,278 --> 00:01:22,171
Under nyc taxi, persist docs, with relation and columns set to true.

20
00:01:22,451 --> 00:01:23,050
Save.

21
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:29,319
Run the project from the Project menu, so dbt rebuilds the models with their comments.

22
00:01:30,269 --> 00:01:31,755
Three models, no errors.

23
00:01:33,469 --> 00:01:35,248
Let's look inside DuckDB.

24
00:01:35,528 --> 00:01:44,047
Open the SQL Editor, pick the nyc taxi dev connection, and ask DuckDB for the columns of trips per month, with their comments.

25
00:01:45,721 --> 00:01:47,121
Run it with the green arrow.

26
00:01:49,900 --> 00:01:53,093
Each column carries the description from schema dot yml.

27
00:01:53,373 --> 00:01:56,163
Average fare has none, because we didn't describe it.

28
00:01:57,113 --> 00:02:05,831
So one description shows up in three places: in the docs site, which we build next lesson, in the database, and for everyone who reads the code.

29
00:02:06,781 --> 00:02:13,604
Back in the project, open the Git tab: two new YAML files, and the change to dbt project dot yml.

30
00:02:14,554 --> 00:02:18,941
Stage all, type a message, describe the models and the zone seed, and commit.

31
00:02:24,153 --> 00:02:26,188
Sync Changes, and it's on GitHub.

32
00:02:29,253 --> 00:02:31,989
To recap: properties are YAML next to your SQL.

33
00:02:32,269 --> 00:02:40,157
Schema dot yml describes the models, seeds dot yml the seed, and persist docs copies the descriptions into DuckDB.

34
00:02:40,437 --> 00:02:42,274
Next, the docs site and the DAG.
